Inspect and maintain exact host-key trust. It observes exactly the endpoints this context declares and records what they present. A Machine that proves its host key another way is reported and left alone; a changed key is superseded only by naming it in --replace.

Usage:
  bootwright machine trust [flags]

Examples:
  bootwright machine trust --context lab --dry-run

Flags:
      --dry-run           Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary
      --machines string   Select comma-separated machine names (default: all)
      --output string     Select output mode (values: text, json) (default "text")
      --replace string    Select comma-separated replacements (default: none)
      --yes               Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines
